ur classification relies on load profiles and developer disclosures, so pleas=
e treat the split as our estimate rather than a reported figure.
- In our data, waits of three to five years are now typical for large loads, =
and requested in-service dates keep slipping as projects are restudied. Power=
 demand is arriving faster than transmission can be built.
